SM(394,{"n":"Deuteronomy 6","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Deuteronomy 6.mp3","d":2872.6,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.04,"Chapter 6. Now these are the commandments, the ordinances, and the judgments the Lord your God commanded to teach you, that you may do them in the land you are crossing over to inherit, and may fear the Lord your God to keep all his commandments."],[35.52,"Keep all his ordinances and commandments I command you today."],[39.12,"You and your sons and the sons of your sons, all the days of your life, so your days may be prolonged."],[45.92,"Therefore, hear, O Israel, and be careful to do it, that it may be well with you, and you may multiply greatly, as the Lord God of your fathers told you, to give you a land flowing with milk and honey."],[56.84,"Okay, so no further suspense."],[59.6,"So Moses then immediately says So here's what he"],[59.81,"God taught Moses all the ordinances, the commandments, etc."],[62.77,"etc. Here's what he gave me to teach you."],[68.69,"Without further ado."],[70.61,"These are the ordinances of the judge."],[72.37,"Well, there's a little more ado."],[73.73,"Uh these are the ordinances of the judgments the Lord commanded the children of Israel in the desert when they came from the land of Egypt."],[81.25,"Now we get to something that you probably have heard before."],[85.01,"Hear, O Israel, the Lord your God is one Lord."],[88.37,"You shall love the Lord your God from your whole heart, from your whole soul, and from your whole power."],[97.17,"So we'll just stop there."],[98.85,"Now, you've probably heard both of those verses, but you probably haven't heard them together all that much."],[104.05,"There's this weird tendency, and the New Testament actually doesn't do this"],[110.41,"When Christ quotes it, he quotes both verses."],[113.13,"But there's this weird tendency for people to just split off the second part."],[118.09,"Love the Lord your God, and the way it is in the New Testament is with all your heart, soul, mind, and strength."],[123.61,"Mind gets added because there's not a word in Hebrew for mind."],[129.29,"So the word uh Dionia, which is in Greek for mind, gets added in the New Testament."],[137.53,"But the rest of it is from here."],[140.09,"But that follows what's called the Shema, because that's the first word in Israel."],[145.77,"Here is Shema."],[148.33,"Uh hero Israel, and yeah, it's translated a certain way here, probably better translated for the Hebrew Hero Israel, Yahweh your God, Yahweh is one."],[159.73,"Which in in Hebrew is uh Shema Yitzrael uh Yahweh Eloheinu Yahweh Echad."],[168.37,"And the reason I gave you the Hebrew is that it's actually important."],[171.25,"Man, all this throat clearing and stuff."],[173.01,"This is gonna be a great recording to edit."],[175.09,"Have fun, ancient faith."],[177.01,"So the Hebrew is kind of important there."],[179.97,"And then the Greek, the way the Greek does it, as it's translated here, is also important for a different reason."],[185.89,"So the reason the Hebrew is important is this has been in modern times, and I mean modern times very literally, like 17th century onward, been considered a statement of what gets called monotheism."],[206.01,"That there's just one God."],[208.17,"Monotheism is a word that was coined in the 17th century."],[213.37,"Now, the reason that could be surprising to you is that monos, meaning one, and theos, meaning God, are both Greek words."],[224.65,"So those two Greek words were around for a long time before they got put together."],[232.89,"Church fathers never used the term monotheism."],[237.13,"Not once. Well, it makes that even weirder is they use the term polytheism, which means many gods, but they never use the term monotheism."],[247.89,"They use the term uh monarchia, meaning there's one first principle."],[255.09,"One thing which is first."],[256.69,"I won't go too far down that rabbit hole."],[259.63,"But just to say that this monotheism category is a very modern, not original category."],[266.59,"But the biggest problem in terms of the Hebrew with interpreting it as that idea."],[272.39,"Saying that here, O Israel, Yahweh your God, Yahweh is one, that that's saying that there's only one God that exists, is the fact that the Hebrew word used here is Ehad."],[283.63,"There are two different words that could be translated into English as one from Hebrew"],[290.71,"One of them is Eh."],[292.23,"It's used here."],[293.27,"The other one is Yahid."],[296.47,"Okay? So Yahid means one in the sense of like the number one."],[305.12,"There's just one of something."],[307.2,"I'm selling you one camel."],[311.54,"Yahid Jamal. Here you go."],[315.27,"So that means the number one."],[317.11,"That's not what's used here."],[320.23,"Ehad means one, like united, like undivided."],[326.23,"Like if I say, uh, here's a biblical example"],[333.15,"Husband and wife become one flesh."],[337.47,"It's not Yahid."],[339.33,"It's Echad. They become one."],[342.63,"They're united. United comes with the word unit, which also means one."],[349.99,"Um, so they become one."],[352.23,"So it is one in that sense."],[356.07,"So, what this is actually saying in the original Hebrew is that Yahweh is undivided."],[366.83,"He is not many."],[369.47,"He's not. separate"],[372.45,"Many separate. And part of the reason that's important is that Eloheinu in there, your God, Eloheinu is through Elohim, which is plural."],[388.82,"So to put this into later theological terminology, this is saying there is one divine nature."],[397.86,"So there are not many different gods."],[400.5,"There are not many different types of God."],[403.22,"God is not made up of a bunch of other gods."],[406.02,"Divinity is not separate."],[409.14,"Their God Yahweh is united and is one"],[413.54,"So this is not a statement of the Trinity, but it also is not a statement that excludes the idea of the Trinity."],[427.0,"The statement that's being made here, and the doctrine of the Trinity are two different things."],[432.76,"They could both be true, both be false, one could be true, one could be false."],[436.82,"They're not, they don't speak to each other per se."],[442.38,"Much to a lot of."],[444.3,"So, well, not to a lot of certain not well educated in their own religion, modern Jewish people."],[451.66,"This causes them a lot of consternation."],[453.74,"They like to quote this as if it says something against. the Trinity"],[457.78,"If they know more about Judaism, they know that even just within Judaism, there are lots of ideas of the Jewish God, where there are aspects of God or God is manifold, or there, you know, the hundred names of God."],[474.36,"There are these different ideas within Judaism."],[480.34,"But those are all acceptable within this the same way the Holy Trinity is, because God is one."],[490.26,"The nature of God is one."],[492.1,"Yeah. Yeah. When you say that, are you referring to like Second temporal Judaism?"],[498.26,"Oh, like in the big case we're just mean or modern both?"],[501.06,"Yeah Yeah. There are certain ideas in Second Temple Judaism that sort of come to flower in Christianity, and so later Judaism gets rid of them."],[511.74,"But even within like modern Judaism, when you look at ideas like the Sephirot and other things."],[518.94,"Yeah, there's a lot of stuff where you're like, you know, or the the way the Shik Shikina is talked about in a lot of Hasidic circles."],[529.34,"There's a there's a lot of things like this where they're gonna talk about different aspects of God that doesn't violate the oneness of God, in their view."],[539.8,"And so by the same token, the Holy Trinity doesn't either."],[544.1,"And that explains why, if you're reading, like the church father's talking about the Trinity, why they make certain distinctions about there being one divine nature."],[552.62,"And what and you're sort of like, well, why are they hammering on this so much?"],[556.46,"Well, it's because of this."],[557.91,"They're trying to say this isn't a contradiction to what scripture says about God here in the Old Testament."],[565.03,"So when Christ talks about this, um, because I don't remember, he doesn't say uh the Shemoth part."],[574.81,"It's as far as I remember, it's depends on which gospel you're reading."],[581.13,"Yeah. Yeah. Because I didn't know if it was a situation where it's like he's more just talking to Richmond."],[586.01,"No, he does the whole thing."],[587.21,"And here's the reason why."],[589.57,"If you have that understanding, you know, well, so why is it saying that?"],[592.45,"We're talking about commandments."],[593.57,"That's not a commandment."],[595.32,"That's a statement."],[596.38,"The second part is the commandment."],[599.02,"But the commandment is related."],[601.5,"Because what is what is the commandment?"],[604.94,"Commandment is you're gonna love Yahweh your God, your whole heart, your whole soul, and your whole power, your whole might."],[613.19,"All your might."],[614.84,"So the statement is God is undivided."],[619.72,"Your love for God needs to be undivided."],[626.22,"That's how those relate."],[629.23,"So God is one and undivided."],[633.03,"Therefore, your love, your loyalty, your faithfulness to God needs to be whole, one, united."],[641.37,"And this is this is a pattern that's all through."],[643.69,"We've already seen this a bunch of times in the Torah, and we're going to keep seeing it in Deuteronomy."],[647.94,"Which says, do not mistreat your slaves because you were slaves in Egypt."],[653.64,"Where there's a statement of sort of fact."],[656.44,"You know what it's like to live in someone else's land."],[659.0,"Therefore, when someone else is living in your land, you treat them."],[662.84,"So this is that same kind of argument."],[664.92,"God is undivided."],[669.56,"Your love for him must be undivided."],[671.96,"The other piece of that is the Greek translation."],[673.16,"the Greek translation. So, of course, they don't transliterate the name Yahweh"],[680.62,"They put Lord, they put Kyrgios."],[683.02,"And so the English translation here is a pretty literal translation of the Greek."],[689.5,"Uh when it says, the Lord your God is one Lord."],[694.06,"Okay, so the reason I'm pointing this out, and you can say in a certain sense that's inaccurate."],[699.44,"I mean, you kind of get the idea he's one, he's united still."],[702.66,"You know, the Lord your God is one Lord."],[705.46,"Is it quite the same?"],[707.14,"But uh in in Colossians, St."],[710.26,"Paul takes this Greek, and you may remember we commented on this at the time."],[715.14,"Way back that was years ago, I know, but uh pepperch Farm remembers that remember Saint Paul says for us there is one God, he uses the same Greek, the Father, and one Lord, Jesus Christ."],[735.62,"So he takes this language, and makes explicit the idea of God the Father, and Christ is God the Son."],[748.4,"And by putting that into the Shema here, he's saying Father and Christ are one, or one God."],[759.1,"So he's explicitly tying the idea of Christ and the Father to this idea of the oneness of God."],[770.2,"The unity. Do we know one, or is it just there?"],[780.36,"There are a few places where it's written as o'on, which is what you see in like iconography, Greek iconography."],[787.8,"But that begs a question too, because that's not transliterated."],[791.56,"That's translated. Okay, you know, Yahweh is a participle in Hebrew, and so O-on is a Greek participle of the verb to be."],[802.76,"Yahweh is a Hebrew participle of the verb to be."],[806.6,"So they're translating it"],[810.24,"And so I think the key element is that the translators and the fathers and the iconographers, everyone who does this, and this is borne out by Saint Dionysius the Aryopagite and St."],[822.24,"Gregory Palomos. So, you know, argue with them, internet."],[827.2,"They treat it not as a name but as a title."],[830.72,"And by that I mean not a proper name."],[833.38,"That it's a title."],[834.9,"It's saying, meaning it's saying something about God."],[838.9,"And ultimately, through Saint Dionysius and St."],[841.78,"Gregory Palomos, all of the names of God are actually divine energies, meaning they're descriptions of God's activity."],[850.5,"It's describ.ing, it's describing God's activity, not his essence"],[855.9,"And so we talked about back in Genesis that Yahweh is actually, for all the inside baseball people in Hebrew, it's a Hiphil participle, meaning it's causative."],[865.9,"So it literally means he who causes to be."],[870.14,"He who causes things to be."],[873.1,"So that's not only the idea of creation."],[877.99,"Obviously, but also as God acting in the world to bring things into being."],[886.11,"And that makes sense then to read that as an energy."],[889.17,"This is one of God's activities."],[892.15,"In his creation."],[893.67,"His causing things that were not before now to be."],[898.07,"And so notice, as we continue, you'll continue to see this, but we'll say this now."],[903.67,"That two part commandment there that we just read."],[907.67,"We're gonna see that's set off."],[909.69,"So we got the Ten Commandments, and then Moses says, okay, here's all the other stuff."],[914.67,"Because you gotta hit pause at that point and said we can't take anymore."],[918.11,"So here's all the other stuff."],[920.28,"But he's also gonna pause after this."],[924.52,"He says this, and then he pauses, and then he's gonna get into specifics again."],[930.12,"And that's why it's not just Christ."],[933.5,"Christ does this in the Gospels, but it's not just him."],[936.22,"This is common by that point to see that that we just read as a summary."],[938.46,"That sort of summarizes everything"],[945.06,"Because if you if you love God with an undivided love."],[952.52,"And it's an undivided love, all your heart, all your soul, all your strength."],[958.92,"So everything you do, everything you think."],[963.64,"If you do that completely and undividedly, you're gonna are are there any of these other commandments that you're gonna break?"],[972.6,"No. So it it summarizes, it sort of summarizes the whole thing."],[977.34,"So when Christ presents this as a summary of the whole Torah of all the commandments.s, He' not just picking a random one"],[985.76,"It's it's set up this way here in Deuteronomy as being a summary."],[989.84,"And this is also where St."],[991.28,"Paul says in Romans, remember he says, the one who loves keeps the whole law."],[995.76,"The one who loves keeps the whole Torah."],[998.48,"Because if you keep this completely, all the others you'll be keeping as well."],[1004.52,"So these words I command you today shall be in your heart and in your soul."],[1010.12,"You shall teach them to your sons, and shall talk of them when you sit in your house, when you walk by the way, when you lie down, and when you rise up."],[1018.92,"You shall bind them as a sign on your hand, and it shall be immovable before your eyes"],[1024.24,"And you shall write them on the doorposts of your houses and on your gates."],[1027.84,"So we know future generations of Jewish people took that very literally."],[1031.7,"But what's what's the idea here?"],[1034.34,"When you sit down, when you stand up, when you lay down in bed, when you get up from bed."],[1038.92,"When you go out, when you come in, when you're walking out the door, when you're walking in the door, when you're that's all the time."],[1044.76,"All the time."],[1046.04,"That's part of the undivided."],[1050.3,"It's not like, oh yes, I have these moments where I really love God fully and completely."],[1056.22,"And then I go do other stuff."],[1059.66,"That's not how that works."],[1061.63,"That's not undivided."],[1064.67,"Not completely. And again, against our tendency, as I said before, we tend to see things very individually as modern people."],[1069.47,"But it's not just important that you have this in your heart and soul"],[1074.84,"It's important that you teach this to your children and your children's children."],[1077.9,"This is generational."],[1078.94,"This is communal."],[1079.74,"This is about everybody."],[1081.58,"That's just about me over against everybody else."],[1083.98,"Well, I'm going to keep all of these commandments so that I'll be one of the good people and not like those bad people."],[1089.98,"That sounds like some people we run into in the gospels who aren't the good guys."],[1094.7,"This is I am going to live these out."],[1098.78,"And I'm going to, through my example and through talking about it, encourage everyone around me to live this way."],[1105.98,"And especially my family members, and especially my children, and especially right said it, so this is a generational thing."],[1112.94,"thing. This is a communal"],[1113.18,"This is something we do as a community together."],[1117.78,"So it shall be when the Lord your God brings you into the land he swore to your fathers to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, to give you large and beautiful cities you did not build, and houses full of all good things you did not fill, and hewn out wells you did not dig, and vineyards and olive groves you did not plant."],[1136.82,"And when you have eaten and are full, then beware."],[1141.7,"That's an interesting."],[1143.75,"Because all this is sounding really good so far."],[1146.87,"Wow, I'm gonna have a well."],[1148.43,"Uh I've been living my whole life out here in this desert."],[1152.71,"And I'm gonna have a well without even having to dig it."],[1155.43,"I'm gonna have a supply of water on my property."],[1159.13,"I'm gonna have vineyards growing grapes that I didn't have to plant and wait and sit, and I'm gonna have graters full of food, I'm gonna have all these."],[1166.09,"This is all sounding really good."],[1167.93,"Thanks, God. Awesome."],[1169.63,"And then when it says you're gonna receive all these wonderful things, beware."],[1174.43,"Beware. Not rejoice."],[1178.15,"Not give thanks."],[1179.67,"Then beware lest you forget the Lord who brings you out from the land of Egypt out of the house of bondage."],[1186.63,"See, God knows them very well."],[1190.01,"God knows them very well."],[1192.09,"God loves to give us good things."],[1195.05,"The problem is a lot of times the good things God gives us turn into a snare for us."],[1200.73,"I would love to win the publisher's clearing house sweepstakes"],[1208.43,"I enter it several times a day, not a joke."],[1212.83,"Online. I have to do something while I'm in the bathroom."],[1215.87,"I do it on my phone."],[1216.83,"I enter the publisher's clearing house sweepstakes several times a day."],[1220.59,"It's only paid off $20 so far in several years of doing this."],[1224.83,"I'd love the, you know, and in my head, it's like I would never have to worry about money again."],[1233.01,"Just buy and pay off the house."],[1235.41,"Pay off all the debt."],[1236.77,"Pay off all the bills."],[1238.69,"Then I could just relax."],[1240.47,"I wouldn't have to worry about all this stuff."],[1242.31,"I wouldn't have to deal with all this stuff."],[1244.72,"So why why won't God let me win the publisher's clearinghouse sweepstakes, darn it?"],[1250.0,"I'd be super responsible."],[1251.6,"I might almost give some of it to charity, maybe if I had any left."],[1255.2,"Um. How many people have you seen who have won huge amounts of money who go on to live that kind of peaceful, successful, pleasant life the rest of their life?"],[1269.97,"Yes. And how it destroyed their families, how it does."],[1275.9,"So we tend to think, we have in our heads, there are good things that could happen to me, like winning 1$.5 million dollars, and there are bad things that could happen to me, like getting sick, or losing money."],[1287.18,"Or on and on"],[1289.64,"Or not having enough."],[1293.72,"And those are basically based on in part on our imagination."],[1301.24,"If it's things we don't have that we wish we had."],[1303.96,"We're imagining what that would be like, and we're usually wrong."],[1308.1,"Or not liking situations we're actually in."],[1313.54,"And wanting to be wanting to be rid of them."],[1318.82,"But the reality is any bad thing that happens to us."],[1326.86,"That we would consider bad."],[1328.06,"That anyone would consider bad."],[1329.52,"Nobody, nobody' likes, yay, I got sick."],[1330.48,"Like, yeah, that's a bad thing"],[1335.3,"But that, depending on how we receive it, depending on how we respond to it, depending on what we learn from it, can actually be a much, much better experience."],[1351.78,"Could be more important, could be a better thing happening to us than one winning 1.5 million dollars, depending on how we receive that and how we act based on that and what that does."],[1364.02,"Right to us and to our our family and to our relationships."],[1369.98,"There is a next level of understanding how God works in our life that I do not claim to have achieved."],[1377.9,"So I'm going to do a St."],[1379.1,"Paul here. I know a man in Christ."],[1380.94,"But I saw a person post this recently, I think I mentioned this on Sunday."],[1385.26,"Who could literally say and mean it, getting cancer was the best thing that ever happened to him."],[1394.06,"You're like, that's insane."],[1396.46,"That is insane."],[1397.42,"Unless you just lived the most horrible life in the history of the world."],[1401.4,"Everything that happened to you was worse than cancer."],[1404.18,"Like, we can't fathom that."],[1406.07,"He had recovered from cancer when he said this 30 years later, and he was looking back on how that experience of having had cancer and gone through cancer treatment and everything involved, how that had changed him as a person, how that had changed how he looked at other people, how he was able to help other people who were struggling, his relationship with God, his race, and and could see that of all the things that had ever happened to him, that was the one that made the biggest positive difference ultimately, ultimately, in the long run, in his life."],[1446.45,"So, this what we have here is talking about the opposite of that."],[1449.81,"This is talking about all these wonderful things God's about to do for Israel that he knows for some of them are gonna turn into a snare."],[1458.85,"Some honesty time."],[1459.81,"I won't ask you to raise hands or actually give me numbers."],[1463.13,"But think in your head, how many times have you gotten sick, prayed, and you've asked God to make you better?"],[1471.29,"You don't have to, well, just have that."],[1473.93,"If you want to, you can have a rough estimate of that number of times in your head."],[1477.93,"Okay? Now I want you to sit next to that estimate number of times in your head, the number of times you've woken up in the morning healthy and thanked God for the fact that you were healthy that day."],[1492.49,"If you're like me, the first number is a lot bigger than the second number."],[1500.19,"The first number is kind of big and the second number is kind of small, especially in comparison."],[1505.55,"We have this amazing ability. to forget God when we think things are going pretty good"],[1513.75,"Then something bad happens, and in case a fire break glass, we run over and break open the God cabinet."],[1520.39,"Please help me."],[1522.09,"Please help me."],[1523.61,"This, by the way, is one of the reasons why sometimes God lets certain bad things, bad things, happen to us."],[1529.85,"I did scare quotes around bad things."],[1533.45,"To get our attention again."],[1536.65,"Because the fact that we think everything's going fine doesn't actually mean everything's fine."],[1543.29,"Doesn't mean everything in me is fine."],[1545.13,"Doesn't mean everything in my relationship with other people is fine."],[1548.89,"It just means I'm kind of cruising."],[1550.97,"Things may be actually very bad, but I'm cruising."],[1555.09,"And so God needs to get my attention."],[1558.77,"We just forget."],[1560.45,"And God points out here one of the perils of us forgetting too, because notice what he keeps reiterating."],[1566.37,"You've got wells that you didn't dig."],[1569.57,"You've got granaries that you didn't fill."],[1571.73,"You've got vineyards you didn't plant."],[1573.89,"Because when they forget about God, what are they going to start thinking?"],[1577.73,"I did it."],[1578.85,"Yes, I did it."],[1581.65,"Started from nothing."],[1582.85,"Now we're here."],[1585.13,"Like, you know?"],[1586.77,"Every politician born in a log cabin, even well into the 20th century, somehow."],[1594.05,"Like, you know, came from nothing, worked their way up. you know, had to borrow money for their first whatever, you know, and then now they're billionaire or whatever"],[1603.77,"Yeah, and of course, you know, if you weren't alive, you wouldn't have been able to do any of that."],[1609.21,"If you weren't healthy, you wouldn't have been able to do any of that."],[1612.01,"If, you know, you you had been uh born in sub Saharan Africa, you probably wouldn't have been able to do that."],[1619.23,"Like born in the wrong part of town."],[1622.76,"Born in the wrong part of town here in the United States."],[1624.68,"Yeah, you were but right."],[1625.64,"There's all kinds of things that could have stopped you all along the way that you were protected from and that God gave you, but you you forgot about him."],[1635.08,"Because everything's going great."],[1637.48,"And so that's the danger that God's pointing at you."],[1640.84,"And why is it? a danger"],[1642.32,"It's not that, oh, God's going to get mad that you forgot about him."],[1647.52,"And you're not giving him the credit."],[1649.46,"It's because what's going to happen when you forget God?"],[1652.5,"You're going to forget all these commandments."],[1654.5,"And what are these commandments?"],[1655.86,"These commandments are telling you how to live if you want to live forever."],[1660.58,"These commandments are telling you to have life."],[1663.54,"And so when you forget them, you're not going to stay on that path."],[1668.1,"You're going to go off to the right, you're going to go off to the left."],[1671.78,"Because you've forgotten about hims,elf so you've also forgotten about what he told you."],[1676.1,"And the advice he gave you."],[1677.86,"In fact, if I accomplished all this myself, whose advice do I really need?"],[1683.38,"Who do I really need to listen to?"],[1685.98,"Clearly it was me and my intelligence and instincts that got me this far."],[1690.96,"So I don't need to listen to anybody."],[1693.2,"I've got it all together."],[1694.86,"So that's the danger."],[1697.42,"And so we have this, on the one hand, this forgetting."],[1702.38,"The other hand, what we read about just before that."],[1705.82,"That these are the things you talk about."],[1707.74,"These are the things you teach your children."],[1709.98,"You talk about with each other."],[1711.74,"That you encourage each other with, that you urge each other on to do."],[1715.6,"Not, oh, congratulations, you got some more money, or hey man, nice car."],[1719.84,"You just pulled up in."],[1721.88,"But I saw how you helped that person who needed help."],[1726.7,"I saw how you sho compwedassion."],[1727.82,"That's impressive I'm impressed by how you know you had a lot of problems with this, but you got your life together, man."],[1735.54,"Those are the things that we encourage and talk to each other about."],[1740.26,"Not like acquiring more stuff."],[1743.64,"Or having more prosperity."],[1746.92,"You shall fear the Lord your God and serve him, and you shall cling to him and take oaths in his name."],[1752.28,"You shall not go after different gods, the gods of the nations around you."],[1756.12,"Because the Lord your God is a jealous God among you, lest the anger of the Lord your God be aroused against you and destroy you from the face of the earth."],[1765.4,"So now, this sounds, especially the way it's translated."],[1769.1,"Oh, he's jealous."],[1770.78,"Oh, they're going around with other gods, I'm angry."],[1774.4,"This is this is not to be taken to be taken literally."],[1779.25,"In the sense that this is God trying to explain something about himself to them."],[1786.69,"People who like us can't fully comprehend God."],[1790.71,"And how God works."],[1792.92,"And these are people who even had to tap out after the Ten Commandments, like we can't even hear any more of this."],[1798.12,"Okay. So God, when he speaks to us, he spoke to them in the Torah in Hebrew, because that was a language that they knew."],[1806.84,"When he taught, and we've talked about this, when he talks about the creation of the world, he doesn't describe it in terms of quantum physics."],[1814.04,"He didn't know quantum physics."],[1814.92,"So he didn't use that kind of language, to describe the creation, the universe"],[1821.3,"He didn't talk about creating photons and have them go, What?"],[1824.12,"Like, everybody assumes that, like, you know, oh, if he was, if if this was really but God, he would have described it in 21st century terms, not 19th or 23rd."],[1836.12,"Like, we've got it."],[1837.72,"But no, God communicates them in language they understand."],[1840.49,"So he's got to communicate to them."],[1844.78,"What is going to be the consequence if you start worshiping these other gods?"],[1850.06,"What what's going to happen to you?"],[1853.26,"And he's talking to a group of people who has no frame of reference for understanding that as being bad."],[1857.98,"They were in Egypt, the Egyptians all worship a bunch of other gods"],[1865.04,"Different parts of Egypt, different cities, they worship different gods."],[1868.24,"All the other nations worship other gods."],[1870.58,"He's kind of got them tentatively on board with okay, you guys are just gonna worship this one."],[1877.28,"Tentatively, kinda. They're not gonna do so well later on, but but they don't have a way to understand, like, if he just said here, he's gonna almost say this later in Deuteronomy, but if he had just said to them right here, all those other gods are demons."],[1894.08,"They're unclean spirits, and if you worship them, uh they're gonna drag your souls to eternal condemnation, they're gonna destroy your humanity."],[1903.89,"They have no frame to understand this."],[1908.85,"Okay, they have no frame to understand what that means."],[1912.45,"What? Now that frame is going to be developed over the course of scripture."],[1919.05,"God is God doesn't just like drop this on them and then leave."],[1925.63,"We have the rest of the Old Testament and then the New Testament, where God brings them to greater understanding, over time."],[1933.61,"Not he changes, but he brings them to a better understanding of the same thing."],[1940.01,"And so here, the quickest and easiest way to explain it to them is right think of God like a husband and Israel like his bride see he doesn't abandon this he uses this analogy all through the scriptures but he's making an analogy to them that they'll understand they're married right they didn't go find a wife they were married off at 13 right to there was an arranged marriage you're married okay imagine your wife with other men and was doing things with other men."],[1977.32,"You would become angry and jealous."],[1981.64,"That would be bad."],[1982.6,"That would destroy your marriage."],[1985.78,"So, by analogy."],[1988.56,"God is the husband."],[1990.8,"They are the bride."],[1991.92,"They are the wife."],[1993.2,"If they go out with these other gods."],[1996.1,"These other men."],[1997.83,"That's gonna destroy the marriage."],[2000.25,"That's gonna destroy this relationship between them and God."],[2005.87,"And that's that's gonna ruin everything."],[2009.13,"Um, and so that's the metaphor."],[2011.53,"He's using this metaphor of adultery."],[2014.65,"But it's a metaphor."],[2015.93,"You say, is God, well, isn't God literally married to Israel?"],[2018.73,"Well, what do you mean by literally?"],[2022.73,"Like, who did the wedding?"],[2024.33,"Like. Like, you can't, of course, that's not literal."],[2028.76,"Like, but that's something within human experience for humans to try to understand the relationship of love, between God and his people."],[2038.48,"And the idea of betraying that love, which is what he's getting at here."],[2044.4,"Yes, sir. And verse before, you didn't build these as well as you didn't build these cities and all the right you with everything."],[2053.84,"Don't go run off."],[2055.12,"Yeah, yeah, yeah."],[2056.4,"Yeah. Yes, sir."],[2058.4,"Um, there's this line about take oaths in his name."],[2062.24,"As an American Protestant, I was taught that that was one of the worst things she could possibly."],[2066.54,"Well, we're gonna get into oaths a little later."],[2068.88,"But the idea is here, and I tried to do the emphasis on the right syllable, but it's take oaths in his name."],[2079.48,"Meaning you're not using the names of other gods, you're not calling upon other gods to do things."],[2088.93,"When you call upon a god, you're calling upon Yahweh."],[2093.17,"So the emphasis is on the his, not on the take."],[2097.97,"He's not commanding them to take oaths."],[2100.63,"But he's saying if if you're taking oaths, you don't take oaths in the names of these other gods."],[2106.17,"Because it was very common in the pagan world."],[2108.73,"You would just invoke different gods for different purposes."],[2113.55,"In different circumstances of life."],[2115.51,"I mean, like business contract, like all the time."],[2118.01,"Because there's no separation of church and state anywhere in the ancient Near East."],[2121.69,"You know, I mean, your day to day business transactions were sealed with an oath to a God."],[2127.62,"And so God is here trying to forbid that not promote oath taking as a general activity."],[2140.02,"And he'll address that more later on."],[2142.72,"He already has a little bit."],[2144.08,"We already saw that there are ways, like if you make a rash oath, there are ways to get out of it and stuff."],[2149.76,"But this is also part of that."],[2153.6,"God always meets the people where they are."],[2157.68,"And then tries to take them right the next bit."],[2162.44,"God doesn't show up to a bunch of bronze age people and say, okay, guys, we're abolishing slavery."],[2170.76,"We're gonna completely redo your economy."],[2172.84,"Let me explain this thing called capitalism or socialism or whatever to you."],[2177.64,"We're switching to that."],[2180.76,"Like he That's not how God operates."],[2185.4,"But he comes to them, he comes in a world where everyone has some form of slavery."],[2190.68,"Which by the way, we still do."],[2192.28,"It's called incarceration."],[2193.56,"But anyway, um, where everyone has some form of slavery, and says, okay, realistically, you everybody I'm talking to here is gonna have slaves"],[2203.4,"you Here's how have to treat them, which is totally differently than the way anyone else treated slaves in the ancient areas."],[2217.35,"He doesn't sort of abolish these things."],[2219.43,"And this is the pattern that the new, we talked about this in the New Testament with St."],[2222.31,"Paul when he's talking about marriage and slavery and these things."],[2225.53,"St. Paul didn't come and say, we're abolishing slavery, equal rights for women, equal pay for equal rights."],[2232.3,"We're just gonna completely throw off the shackles of the Roman Empire and create a utopian socialist commune in the name of Christianity."],[2240.43,"He says, yes, these are the societal relationships, but here's how you as a Christian have to operate within them."],[2248.57,"And that's fundamentally different than the way other people do."],[2254.17,"And for him, because now we've come into the era of zealotry and stuff in Israel, for St."],[2259.93,"Paul, it's innately anti revolutionary violence."],[2266.17,"Sorry, founding fathers."],[2268.81,"It is, you do not know you operate as a Christian within whatever structures you find yourself."],[2275.89,"So whether you love capitalism or hate capitalism, if you're living in the United States, you're living under capitalism."],[2281.73,"So how do you operate within a capitalist society and world as a Christian?"],[2286.85,"And that's going to look different than the way other people do."],[2291.37,"Or should look different than the way other people do."],[2295.21,"Let's finish up this chapter."],[2296.89,"You shall not tempt the Lord your God as you tempted him in the temptation."],[2300.97,"That is not a great translation."],[2302.97,"You shall not tempt the Lord your God as you tempted him in the temptation."],[2306.65,"You shall that's that is referring to the golden calf."],[2310.33,"That's um, but it's using that as emblematic of a lot of things that happened in the desert."],[2317.85,"I missed something."],[2319.13,"What is emblematic of the golden calf?"],[2322.01,"With the golden calf."],[2322.69,"They incident with the golden calf."],[2324.09,"There are a whole bunch of incidents like that."],[2326.81,"Where they were rebellious in various ways."],[2330.43,"The desert. That's sort of the Sinqua non of them."],[2333.79,"But it's also an exemplar of a type of thing that they did a lot in the desert."],[2339.67,"Now notice the use of the word temptation."],[2343.75,"This is important because this Greek word gets translated temptation all over the place, including in the New Testament."],[2350.63,"And in some places that's misleading."],[2352.95,"Because what do you mean tempt God?"],[2356.71,"God can't be tempted to sin."],[2360.12,"And that's how we hear temptation."],[2362.44,"Much better translation of that verb is test."],[2367.64,"It's really saying do not test God, do not put the Lord your God to the test."],[2372.84,"So, in the same way that we're told in the New Testament explicitly that God tempts no one."],[2377.8,"God. Yet we see testing, say, Abraham"],[2384.38,"This is what God tests all the time."],[2386.76,"But God test testing someone, testing Job is not him tempting them to sin."],[2391.64,"He's not trying to lure them into sinning, the way we think of temptation."],[2397.08,"And testing also is not like taking a test at school."],[2404.36,"This is another bad association we have."],[2407.45,"So if I give you a test at school, I am attempting to determine how much of the knowledge I tried to teach you actually made it through."],[2416.97,"How much of it did you actually learn and retain?"],[2420.03,"And until I get your test turned in and look at it and grade it, I don't know the answer to my question."],[2427.27,"I don't know how much of it I successfully communicated to you."],[2430.95,"Until I get that test back and I look."],[2433.03,"So obviously that doesn't apply to God because God doesn't need to like give someone a test and see the results to know."],[2440.89,"He didn't have to tell Abraham to go sacrifice Isaac in order to know whether he would or not."],[2450.3,"God knew he would."],[2452.22,"Okay, so he's not testing him in that sense."],[2454.7,"Testing here is testing in the sense that like a blacksmith tests a piece of metal."],[2461.42,"So when you take something and you put it in fire to look for impurities and weaknesses."],[2464.94,"es. You test it, you look for impuriti, you look for weakness, you apply pressure to it"],[2472.42,"And the process of doing that strengthens the metal."],[2477.38,"So, as we talked about when we talked about Abraham being told to go and sacrifice Isaac, Abraham doing this, Abraham having this experience strengthens him."],[2487.38,"He learned certain things from it."],[2490.28,"By being put to the test."],[2492.92,"Or you can think of it as like if I asked, probably maybe one or two people in this room might know, but if I asked people in this room, most of us would not know, hey, how fast could you run 50 yards?"],[2507.64,"Well, why I could tell you not very fast, but I couldn't give you an exact number."],[2514.37,"Well, because I haven't I haven't tried."],[2517.17,"Well, trial and test are the same."],[2520.26,"But I could go out in the parking lot."],[2524.16,"Set a stopwatch on my phone."],[2526.62,"Have somebody pace off 50 yards, and we could find out."],[2530.68,"We test I can find out."],[2531.72,"Hey, I now know how fast I can run 50 yards."],[2536.12,"I've learned something about myself."],[2539.41,"Or how much could I bench press right now?"],[2541.49,"I don't know."],[2541.97,"It's been a long time since I tried to bench press anything."],[2544.35,"Unless you count getting out of bed when I'm on my stomach."],[2547.31,"Um, that's more of a push-up."],[2549.39,"But um. I'd have to go and try."],[2555.59,"I'd have to go and try."],[2556.55,"And then I would learn something about myself in that process."],[2559.43,"I might be in better shape or worse shape than I thought I was."],[2563.91,"Testing is about this kind of experience."],[2566.39,"Now, God doesn't have anything to learn about himself."],[2570.79,"And so they're not doing God a favor if they put God to the test."],[2575.91,"They try to put pressure on God."],[2578.31,"Try to put heat on God."],[2579.85,"If they try to."],[2582.77,"What ends this ends up being a disaster for them."],[2587.01,"And so he's saying, you remember that?"],[2591.69,"You remember how well that went?"],[2595.5,"Every time they tried to push God."],[2599.63,"Every time they say, oh, he just brought us out here to die."],[2603.93,"He doesn't give us any meat."],[2605.37,"Yes. Every time they thought they're like the meat with the quail, they were buried in rotting quail."],[2610.86,"God would give them what they thought they wanted and they hate it."],[2615.31,"Um God is saying, do not keep repeating this pattern."],[2618.91,"This was a repeated pattern all through the wilderness."],[2621.17,"And Moses is saying, hey, let's be done with that."],[2627.11,"Let's be done with that."],[2628.87,"If you test God, he won't he won't be found wanting, but it won't go well with you."],[2635.35,"you. You shall diligently keep the commandments of the Lord your God, his testimonies and the ordinances he commanded"],[2642.67,"So you shall do what is pleasing and good before the Lord your God, that it may be well with you, and you may go in and inherit the good land the Lord swore to your fathers, to chase out all your enemies from before your face, as he said."],[2655.81,"And so again, it's not you will keep all these commandments and then he won't be angry at you."],[2662.05,"You will keep all these commandments and then he won't smite you."],[2665.17,"Because these are people who survived the desert."],[2667.31,"That's not everybody got eaten like Korah."],[2669.56,"It is, if you keep these commandments and ordinances, it will go well with you."],[2674.6,"Your life will be good."],[2676.36,"You'll receive the good things of God, in your life."],[2679.86,"Even when, and so people say, Well, wait, does that mean nothing bad will ever happen to you?"],[2686.02,"And I say, Yes, it means nothing bad will ever happen to you."],[2689.3,"Because everything that happens to you, you won't see is bad."],[2693.3,"If everything that happens to you causes you to learn and grow and grow closer to God and understand yourself better and grow in your relationships with other people, then it's not bad."],[2706.18,"Ultimately. So, yes, if you follow God completely and keep all of his commandments, nothing bad will ever happen to you."],[2714.1,"Because nothing that ever happens to you will be bad."],[2719.0,"Because you'll understand."],[2721.08,"Then it shall be when your son asks you tomorrow, saying, What are the testimonies, the ordinances, and the judgments the Lord our God commanded you?"],[2730.72,"You shall say to your son, We were servants of Pharaoh in Egypt, and the Lord brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand and an outstretched arm, and the Lord set great and evil signs aflit affecting Egypt, Pharaoh and his house before us."],[2746.88,"Then he brought us out from there, that he might bring us in to give us this land he swore to give our fathers."],[2753.6,"So the Lord commanded us to do all these ordinances, to fear the Lord our God, that it may be well with us all our days, and we may live as today."],[2762.72,"Then we shall have mercy if we are careful to do all these commandments before the Lord our God is the Lord commanded us."],[2769.12,"So remember, Moses is not going to be there"],[2773.78,"Moses is going over this for the last time."],[2776.9,"So tomorrow, when Moses is gone, and your son asks you, you need to tell him."],[2784.18,"And notice it's we."],[2786.98,"Son, we were slaves in Egypt."],[2790.98,"Not your grandparents."],[2793.75,"We. God brought us out."],[2797.11,"He brought us out of the bondage, out of the slavery that we were in."],[2803.19,"He brought us to where we are now."],[2804.87,"He gave us all of this."],[2807.08,"And he's showed us how to live so we can continue to live, prosper, and thrive. and enjoy this generation after generation"],[2818.0,"And so that still holds today."],[2821.2,"We're a little less literal about Pharaoh in Egypt."],[2824.48,"A little more about having been slaves to sin."],[2827.92,"Powers of darkness, represented by Pharaoh in Egypt, but"],[2831.37,"God has set us free."],[2833.37,"He's brought us to this good place."],[2836.35,"Given us all of these things."],[2838.53,"We share that together, teach that to our children."],[2843.73,"So we'll go ahead and leave off there for now."],[2847.01,"But thank you, everybody."],[2850.13,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2855.25,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com"],[2862.89,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.04,"lv":2,"h":"6:1-3 - What Moses is about to teach","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Deut 6</b> opens: the <b>commandments, ordinances, judgments</b> God commanded Moses to teach</li><li class=\"d1\">purpose: <b>do them</b> in the land they are crossing into; <b>fear the Lord</b></li><li class=\"d1\">all the days of your life - you, sons, <b>sons of your sons</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"that it may be well with you\"</b>; land <b>flowing with milk and honey</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"No further suspense\" - Moses: <b>here's what he gave me to teach you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Without further ado\" - well, <b>a little more ado</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ordinances given to Israel in the desert after coming out of Egypt</li></ul>"},{"t":81.25,"lv":2,"h":"6:4-5 - The Shema","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Hear, O Israel, the Lord your God is one Lord. You shall love the Lord your God...\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Both verses are familiar - rarely <b>together</b></li><li class=\"d1\">weird tendency to split off just the <b>second part</b> (the love)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Christ quotes both</b> verses - NT doesn't split them</li><li class=\"d0\">NT: heart, soul, <b>mind</b>, strength</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>mind</b> added - no Hebrew word for mind; Greek <i>dianoia</i></li><li class=\"d1\">rest comes from here</li><li class=\"d0\">Called the <b>Shema</b> - first word in Hebrew</li><li class=\"d1\"><i>Shema Yisrael, Yahweh Eloheinu, Yahweh echad</i></li><li class=\"d1\">better: \"Hear, O Israel, <b>Yahweh your God, Yahweh is one</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Hebrew matters; the <b>Greek</b> matters for a different reason</li></ul>"},{"t":185.89,"lv":2,"h":"Not a statement of \"monotheism\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Modern times (<b>17th c.</b> onward): read as <b>monotheism</b> - just one God exists</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Monotheism</b> coined in the <b>17th century</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><i>monos</i> + <i>theos</i> both Greek - existed long before being combined</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Church fathers never used it</b> - \"not once\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they used <i>polytheism</i> = many gods, but never monotheism</li><li class=\"d1\">they said <i>monarchia</i> = one <b>first principle</b>, one thing which is first</li><li class=\"d0\">So monotheism is a \"very modern, not original category\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Biggest problem with that reading: the Hebrew word <b><i>echad</i></b></li></ul>"},{"t":266.59,"lv":3,"h":"<i>Echad</i> vs <i>yachid</i>","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two Hebrew words for \"one\": <b><i>echad</i></b> (used here) and <b><i>yachid</i></b></li><li class=\"d0\"><i>Yachid</i> = <b>number one</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm selling you one camel\" - <i>yachid gamal</i></li><li class=\"d0\"><i>Echad</i> = one as <b>united, undivided</b></li><li class=\"d1\">husband and wife become <b>one flesh</b> - <i>echad</i>, not <i>yachid</i></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>united</b> - comes with <b>unit</b>, which also means one</li><li class=\"d0\">So the Shema says <b>Yahweh is undivided</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he is <b>not many</b>, not many separate</li></ul>"},{"t":372.45,"lv":3,"h":"One divine nature","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><i>Eloheinu</i> - your God - from <i>Elohim</i>, which is <b>plural</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Later theological terms: <b>one divine nature</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not many different gods</li><li class=\"d1\">not many types of God</li><li class=\"d1\">God not made up of a bunch of other gods</li><li class=\"d1\">divinity not <b>separate</b>; Yahweh is <b>united and one</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not a statement of the Trinity</b> - but doesn't <b>exclude</b> it</li><li class=\"d1\">the statement and the doctrine are <b>two different things</b></li><li class=\"d1\">both could be true, both false, one true one false - they \"don't speak to each other per se\"</li></ul>"},{"t":442.38,"lv":2,"h":"Modern Judaism and the Trinity","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Causes <b>consternation</b> for modern Jewish people not well educated in their own religion</li><li class=\"d1\">they quote it as if it's <b>against the Trinity</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Those who know Judaism: lots of ideas of God - <b>aspects</b>, <b>manifold</b>, the <b>hundred names</b></li><li class=\"d1\">all acceptable because <b>God is one</b>, nature of God is one</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: do you mean Second Temple or modern Judaism?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>both</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Second Temple ideas that <b>flower in Christianity</b> - later Judaism <b>gets rid of</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">even modern: the <b><i>Sephirot</i></b>; the <b><i>Shekinah</i></b> in Hasidic circles</li><li class=\"d1\">different aspects of God - <b>doesn't violate oneness</b> in their view</li><li class=\"d0\">By the same token, <b>the Trinity doesn't either</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why fathers hammer on <b>one divine nature</b> - showing no contradiction with OT</li></ul>"},{"t":565.03,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: Christ quotes the whole Shema","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: does Christ quote just the commandment part, or all of it?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"No, he does the whole thing\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why: it's a <b>statement</b>, not a commandment</li><li class=\"d1\">second part is the <b>commandment</b> - but they're related</li><li class=\"d0\">Commandment: love Yahweh <b>whole heart, soul, might</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Statement:</b> God is <b>undivided</b> → <b>your love must be undivided</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God one and undivided → your <b>loyalty, faithfulness</b> whole, one, united</li><li class=\"d0\">Pattern all through the Torah, continuing in Deut</li><li class=\"d1\">parallel: do not mistreat slaves because <b>you were slaves in Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d1\">statement of fact → therefore how you act</li><li class=\"d1\">same argument here</li></ul>"},{"t":671.96,"lv":2,"h":"The Greek: \"one Lord\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Greek translation doesn't transliterate <b>Yahweh</b> - puts <b><i>Kyrios</i></b>, Lord</li><li class=\"d1\">English here = literal translation of the Greek: \"the Lord your God is <b>one Lord</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">in a sense less accurate - still gets the idea he's united</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Colossians</b> - St. Paul takes this Greek (\"remember we commented on it years ago\")</li><li class=\"d1\">\"for us there is <b>one God, the Father</b>, and <b>one Lord, Jesus Christ</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Makes explicit: God the Father, Christ = God the Son</li><li class=\"d1\">putting it into the Shema: <b>Father and Christ are one</b> God</li><li class=\"d1\">explicitly ties Christ and Father to the <b>oneness / unity of God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":770.2,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: the name Yahweh - <i>ho on</i>","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: do we know how the name is rendered?</li><li class=\"d1\">sometimes <b><i>ho on</i></b> - seen in <b>Greek iconography</b></li><li class=\"d1\">that's <b>translated</b>, not transliterated</li><li class=\"d0\">Yahweh = <b>Hebrew participle</b> of \"to be\"; <i>ho on</i> = <b>Greek participle</b> of \"to be\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Translators, fathers, iconographers treat it as a <b>title, not a proper name</b></li><li class=\"d1\">borne out by <b>St. Dionysius the Areopagite</b> and <b>St. Gregory Palamas</b> - \"argue with them, internet\"</li><li class=\"d1\">says something <b>about</b> God</li><li class=\"d0\">All names of God = <b>divine energies</b> - his <b>activity</b>, not his essence</li><li class=\"d0\">Genesis: Yahweh is a <b>Hiphil participle</b> = <b>causative</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"he who <b>causes to be</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not only creation - God acting in the world to <b>bring things into being</b></li><li class=\"d1\">fits as an <b>energy</b>: causing things that were not to now be</li></ul>"},{"t":898.07,"lv":2,"h":"The Shema as summary of the Torah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two-part commandment is <b>set off</b></li><li class=\"d1\">after Ten Commandments (\"hit pause - can't take any more\"), Moses gives the rest</li><li class=\"d1\">pauses <b>again</b> after this, then back to specifics</li><li class=\"d0\">Not just Christ - <b>common by then</b> to use it as a <b>summary</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Undivided love: <b>all heart, soul, strength</b> - everything you do, everything you think</li><li class=\"d1\">do it completely → any other commandment you'd break? <b>No</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So Christ isn't picking a random one - <b>set up this way in Deuteronomy</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Romans</b>: \"the one who loves keeps the whole law\"</li><li class=\"d1\">keep this completely → keep all the others</li></ul>"},{"t":1004.52,"lv":2,"h":"6:6-9 - Words in heart, taught to sons","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"These words I command you today shall be in your <b>heart</b> and <b>soul</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Teach sons; talk when you <b>sit, walk, lie down, rise up</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Bind as <b>sign on hand</b>, <b>immovable before your eyes</b>; write on <b>doorposts and gates</b></li><li class=\"d1\">later Jewish generations took it <b>very literally</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Idea: <b>all the time</b> - going out, coming in</li><li class=\"d1\">part of the <b>undivided</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"moments where I really love God fully\" then go do other stuff - <b>not undivided</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Against our <b>modern individual</b> view</li><li class=\"d1\">must <b>teach children and children's children</b> - <b>generational, communal</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"I'll keep these so I'm one of the <b>good people</b>\" - sounds like <b>bad guys in the gospels</b></li><li class=\"d1\">live it out, encourage everyone around me - <b>family, children</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1117.78,"lv":2,"h":"6:10-12 - \"Beware\" when you are full","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Land promised to <b>Abraham, Isaac, Jacob</b>: <b>cities you did not build</b>, houses full of good things, <b>wells you did not dig</b>, vineyards and olive groves you did not plant</li><li class=\"d0\">\"When you have eaten and are full, then <b>beware</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sounds great so far - well without digging, grapes without planting, \"Thanks, God. Awesome.\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but: <b>beware</b> - not rejoice, not give thanks</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Beware lest you <b>forget the Lord</b> who brought you out of Egypt, the house of bondage\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God <b>knows them very well</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he loves to give good things</li><li class=\"d1\">problem: good things <b>turn into a snare</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1200.73,"lv":2,"h":"Sweepstakes: good things and bad things","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Publishers Clearing House - enters several times a day on his phone</li><li class=\"d1\">paid off <b>$20</b> so far</li><li class=\"d1\">in my head: pay off house, debt, bills, <b>relax</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"why won't God let me win?\" - \"I'd be super responsible\"</li><li class=\"d0\">How many big winners live peaceful, successful lives?</li><li class=\"d1\">how it <b>destroyed families</b></li><li class=\"d0\">We sort things into <b>good</b> (win $1.5M) and <b>bad</b> (sick, lose money, not enough)</li><li class=\"d1\">based partly on <b>imagination</b> - what we don't have, we picture - <b>usually wrong</b></li><li class=\"d1\">or not liking situations we're in</li><li class=\"d0\">Any bad thing - <b>depending on how we receive and respond and what we learn</b> - can be a <b>much better experience</b></li><li class=\"d1\">could be <b>more important</b> than winning $1.5M</li></ul>"},{"t":1369.98,"lv":3,"h":"\"Cancer was the best thing that ever happened\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"A next level of understanding how God works... I do not claim to have achieved\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I know a man in Christ\" - St. Paul move</li><li class=\"d0\">Person's post: <b>getting cancer was the best thing that ever happened to him</b>, and meant it</li><li class=\"d1\">\"That is insane\" - unless life was horrible</li><li class=\"d1\">said it <b>30 years after</b> recovering</li><li class=\"d1\">changed him as a person, how he sees others, how he helps struggling people, <b>his relationship with God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">of everything that happened, the one with the <b>biggest positive difference</b> in the long run</li><li class=\"d0\">Deut talks about the <b>opposite</b>: wonderful things God is about to do that will become a <b>snare</b> for some</li></ul>"},{"t":1458.85,"lv":3,"h":"Prayers for health vs. thanks for health","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Honesty time\" - number in your head:</li><li class=\"d1\">times you got sick, prayed, asked God to make you better</li><li class=\"d1\">vs. times you woke up healthy and <b>thanked God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">first number a lot bigger</li><li class=\"d0\">Amazing ability to <b>forget God when things go pretty well</b></li><li class=\"d1\">then something bad → \"<b>in case of fire, break glass</b>\" - break open the God cabinet: \"Please help me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">One reason God lets certain \"bad things\" happen: <b>to get our attention</b></li><li class=\"d1\">things going fine ≠ <b>everything is fine</b> - in me, in relationships</li><li class=\"d1\">\"just cruising\" - may be actually very bad</li><li class=\"d1\">\"We just forget\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1560.45,"lv":3,"h":"The danger: \"I did it\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">God keeps reiterating: wells you didn't dig, granaries you didn't fill, vineyards you didn't plant</li><li class=\"d0\">Forget God → start thinking <b>\"I did it\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"started from nothing, now we're here\" - <b>every politician born in a log cabin</b></li><li class=\"d1\">but: if not alive, not healthy, born in <b>sub-Saharan Africa</b>, wrong part of town - couldn't have done it</li><li class=\"d1\">all kinds of things could have stopped you - <b>God protected you</b>, you forgot</li><li class=\"d0\">Danger is <b>not</b> that God gets mad at no credit</li><li class=\"d1\">you'll <b>forget the commandments</b> - they tell you <b>how to live forever</b>, to have <b>life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">you'll go <b>off to the right, off to the left</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"If I accomplished all this myself, whose advice do I need?\" - \"I've got it all together\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1697.42,"lv":3,"h":"What we should encourage each other in","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">On one hand forgetting; on the other, what we just read: <b>talk about these things</b></li><li class=\"d1\">teach children, talk with each other, <b>urge each other on</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"congratulations on the money\" or \"nice car\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but: \"I saw how you <b>helped that person</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I saw your <b>compassion</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"you had a lot of problems but <b>got your life together</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Those are the things to encourage - <b>not more stuff or prosperity</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1746.92,"lv":2,"h":"6:13-15 - Fear, serve, cling; a jealous God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Fear the Lord and serve him, <b>cling to him</b>, take oaths in his name\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not go after <b>other gods</b> of the nations around you</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The Lord your God is a <b>jealous God</b>\" - anger aroused, destroy you from the face of the earth</li><li class=\"d0\">Sounds like \"he's jealous, I'm angry\" - <b>not to be taken literally</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>explaining something about himself</b> to people who can't fully comprehend him</li><li class=\"d1\">people who had to <b>tap out after the Ten Commandments</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Speaks in <b>Hebrew</b>, a language they knew</li><li class=\"d1\">creation not described with <b>quantum physics</b> - \"didn't talk about photons\"</li><li class=\"d1\">people assume real God would use 21st-c. terms - <b>no</b>, he communicates in language they understand</li><li class=\"d0\">Must tell them the <b>consequence</b> of worshiping other gods</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no frame of reference</b> - Egypt worshiped many gods, different cities different gods; all nations did</li><li class=\"d1\">only <b>tentatively</b> on board with one God</li></ul>"},{"t":1877.28,"lv":3,"h":"Why not just say \"demons\"?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Could have said: \"all those gods are <b>demons</b>, unclean spirits, drag your souls to eternal condemnation\"</li><li class=\"d1\">he'll <b>almost say this later in Deuteronomy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they have <b>no frame to understand</b> it</li><li class=\"d0\">Frame <b>developed over the course of Scripture</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God doesn't drop it and leave - rest of OT and NT bring <b>greater understanding over time</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"not he changes\" - better understanding of the <b>same thing</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1940.01,"lv":2,"h":"Husband and bride analogy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Quickest way: <b>God = husband, Israel = bride</b></li><li class=\"d1\">analogy used <b>all through Scripture</b></li><li class=\"d0\">They'd understand marriage - <b>arranged, married off at 13</b></li><li class=\"d1\">imagine your wife with other men → <b>angry and jealous</b>, destroys the marriage</li><li class=\"d0\">By analogy: going out with <b>other gods = other men</b> → destroys the relationship with God</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Metaphor of adultery</b> - but a metaphor</li><li class=\"d1\">\"isn't God literally married to Israel?\" - \"who did the wedding?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">something within <b>human experience</b> to grasp the <b>relationship of love</b> between God and his people</li><li class=\"d1\">and the idea of <b>betraying that love</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2044.4,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: \"take oaths in his name\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: American Protestant taught oaths were <b>among the worst things</b> - what's this?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"We're gonna get into oaths a little later\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Emphasis on <b>his</b>, not on <i>take</i></li><li class=\"d1\">not commanding oaths - <b>if</b> you take oaths, <b>not in names of other gods</b></li><li class=\"d1\">means: when you call on a god, you call on <b>Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Pagan world: invoke <b>different gods for different purposes</b></li><li class=\"d1\">business contracts, all the time</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no separation of church and state</b> in the ancient Near East - daily transactions sealed with an oath to a god</li><li class=\"d0\">God forbidding that, <b>not promoting oath-taking</b></li><li class=\"d1\">addressed more later; already saw ways out of a <b>rash oath</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2153.6,"lv":2,"h":"God meets people where they are","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"God <b>always meets the people where they are</b>\" - then takes them to the next bit</li><li class=\"d0\">Doesn't show up to bronze-age people: \"we're <b>abolishing slavery</b>, redoing your economy, <b>capitalism or socialism</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">world where everyone has <b>some form of slavery</b> - \"we still do: <b>incarceration</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">says: you will have slaves; <b>here's how to treat them</b> - totally different from anyone else</li><li class=\"d0\">Same pattern in NT: <b>St. Paul</b> on marriage and slavery</li><li class=\"d1\">didn't say abolish slavery, equal rights, throw off Rome, \"utopian socialist commune\"</li><li class=\"d1\">said: these are the structures, <b>here's how you as a Christian operate within them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">era of <b>zealotry</b> - for Paul, innately <b>anti revolutionary violence</b> - \"sorry, founding fathers\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Live under capitalism? <b>How do you operate as a Christian within it</b> - should look <b>different</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2295.21,"lv":2,"h":"6:16 - Do not test the Lord","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"You shall not <b>tempt</b> the Lord your God as you tempted him in the temptation\" - \"not a great translation\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Refers to the <b>golden calf</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Q: what's emblematic? - <b>incident with the golden calf</b>, plus many like it</li><li class=\"d1\">various <b>rebellions</b> in the desert; golden calf the <i>sine qua non</i> and an <b>exemplar</b> of a type of thing they did a lot</li></ul>"},{"t":2339.67,"lv":3,"h":"Tempt vs. test","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Greek word translated <b>temptation</b> all over, incl. NT - sometimes <b>misleading</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God can't be tempted to sin</li><li class=\"d1\">better verb: <b>test</b> - \"do not put the Lord your God to the test\"</li><li class=\"d0\">NT: <b>God tempts no one</b> - yet he <b>tests</b> (Abraham, Job)</li><li class=\"d1\">not luring them into sin</li><li class=\"d0\">Testing is <b>not like a school test</b></li><li class=\"d1\">school test: teacher finds out how much got through - doesn't know until graded</li><li class=\"d1\">God doesn't need results - didn't need Abraham to sacrifice Isaac to <b>know</b>; \"God knew he would\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Testing = <b>blacksmith testing metal</b>: fire, look for <b>impurities and weaknesses</b>, pressure</li><li class=\"d1\">process <b>strengthens the metal</b>; Abraham <b>learned from it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Or: how fast can I run <b>50 yards</b>? how much can I bench?</li><li class=\"d1\">\"trial and test are the same\" - go to the parking lot, stopwatch, <b>learn something about myself</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God has <b>nothing to learn</b> about himself</li><li class=\"d1\">put <b>pressure and heat on God</b> → disaster for them</li><li class=\"d1\">every time: \"he brought us out here to die\", no meat → <b>buried in rotting quail</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God gave what they thought they wanted - <b>they hated it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: <b>repeated pattern</b> through the wilderness - \"let's be done with that\"</li><li class=\"d1\">if you test God, he won't be found wanting - <b>but it won't go well with you</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2635.35,"lv":2,"h":"6:17-19 - Keep the commandments","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Diligently keep commandments, testimonies, ordinances; <b>do what is pleasing and good</b> → well with you, <b>inherit the good land</b>, enemies chased out as he said</li><li class=\"d0\">Not: keep them and <b>he won't be angry / won't smite you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">these are people who <b>survived the desert</b> - not eaten like <b>Korah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if you keep them, <b>it will go well with you</b>, receive the <b>good things of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: does that mean <b>nothing bad will ever happen</b>? - \"<b>Yes</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">because everything that happens, you won't see as bad</li><li class=\"d1\">if it makes you <b>learn, grow, draw close to God</b>, know yourself, grow in relationships → <b>not bad</b></li><li class=\"d1\">follow God completely → <b>nothing that happens will be bad</b>, because you'll understand</li></ul>"},{"t":2721.08,"lv":2,"h":"6:20-25 - When your son asks","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"When your son asks you <b>tomorrow</b>: what are the testimonies, ordinances, judgments?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">answer: \"<b>We</b> were servants of Pharaoh in Egypt\" - <b>mighty hand and outstretched arm</b>, signs and wonders</li><li class=\"d1\">brought us out to bring us in; commanded us to fear the Lord → <b>well with us all our days</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"it shall be <b>mercy</b> (righteousness) for us if we are careful to do all these commandments\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses going over this <b>for the last time</b> - won't be there <b>tomorrow</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Notice <b>\"we\"</b>: \"Son, <b>we</b> were slaves in Egypt\" - not your grandparents</li><li class=\"d1\">God brought <b>us</b> out of bondage, gave us all this, showed how to live so we <b>prosper generation after generation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Still holds today</li><li class=\"d1\">less literal about Pharaoh and Egypt - more about <b>slaves to sin</b>, <b>powers of darkness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God has <b>set us free</b>, brought us to a good place - <b>teach that to our children</b></li></ul>"}]});
